     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg for extended-release in the US). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up a lot, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nMaybe the dose was a typo or a mix-up with the total daily amount. These are some options I can enter:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day. This is the labeled maximum for IR.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, for 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day, split into doses**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- A lower starting dose, such as 500 mg twice daily, if the patient is new to metformin. You can titrate it up.\n\nTell me which you want, or give me the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
